      "message": "Suggestion: this loop is searching for inventory path match. We can refactor this using C++23 `std::ranges::find_if()`. Something like:\n\n```\nconst std::string\u0026 l_fruPath \u003d l_fru.key();\n    const auto\u0026 l_entries \u003d l_fru.value();\n\n    // C++23 style predicate search\n    auto l_it \u003d std::ranges::find_if(l_entries, [\u0026i_inventoryPath](const auto\u0026 l_entry) {\n        return l_entry.value(\"inventoryPath\", \"\") \u003d\u003d i_inventoryPath;\n    });\n    ```\n    \n1. This will eliminate a level of indentation\n2. Standard algorithms are thoroughly tested, exception-safe, and handle edge cases (like empty containers) cleanly.\n3. Performance overhead remains unaffected.",
